    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>RAII wrapper for database connection lifecycle management.</para>
<para>Ensures database connections are returned to the pool on destruction, preventing resource exhaustion in both normal and exception paths.</para>
<para>Usage: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">const</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>connection_id<sp/>=<sp/>acquireConnectionId();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>guard<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="classthemisdb_1_1analytics_1_1_connection_guard_1a10226090117980ee75f9804dea2617c7" kindref="member">ConnectionGuard::acquire</ref>(</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>connection_id,</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>[&amp;]<sp/>{<sp/>releaseConnection(connection_id);<sp/>});</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>executeQuery();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Connection<sp/>automatically<sp/>released<sp/>when<sp/>guard<sp/>goes<sp/>out<sp/>of<sp/>scope</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>SAFETY: This guard is exception-safe. Even if an exception is thrown after acquiring the connection, the destructor will release it. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
